IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cla-core`

-- Civil Liability Act 2002 (NSW) -- Part 1B (child abuse: liability of organisations, ss 6A-6P) and Part 1C (child
-- abuse: setting aside settlements, ss 7A-7F), with the Schedule 1 clauses that time them (cll 43-45).
--
-- SEAT: the person who was abused as a child, suing (or about to sue) an organisation. Every exported question is one
-- that person would ask: "Did the organisation owe me the duty, and is it presumed to have breached it?", "Is the
-- organisation vicariously liable?", "Can I sue an unincorporated organisation, and who answers for it?", "By when must
-- it name its trusts?", "Can my old settlement be set aside?". The organisation, its trustees and the court get no seat.
--
-- Out: s 6Q (rules of court: machinery); s 6I (objects); s 6P(5) (Corporations Act displacement: not a question the
-- claimant asks); the regulations that may prescribe associated individuals (s 6E(1)(c)), akin-to-employee circumstances
-- (s 6G(4)) and matters for reasonable precautions (s 6F(4)(h)): none deposited, noted in NOTES.md.
--
-- Based on content from the New South Wales Legislation website (as collected by the Open Australian Legal Corpus on
-- 10 March 2025, corpus version dated 16 June 2022; unofficial, possibly out of date). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not
-- for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Civil Liability Act 2002 -- Parts 1B and 1C`

§§ `The nouns`

-- s 6F(5), s 6H(4): "child abuse ... means sexual abuse or physical abuse ... but does not include an act that is lawful
-- at the time it takes place". s 6J "child abuse proceedings" is wider: "abuse (including sexual abuse) against a child".
DECLARE `Kind of abuse` IS ONE OF
    `sexual abuse`
    `physical abuse`
    `another kind of abuse, such as emotional or psychological abuse or neglect`

-- s 6D: "an organisation is responsible for a child if it (including any part of it) exercises care, supervision or
-- authority over the child (or purports to do so or is obliged by law to do so)", and (b) where it delegates that
-- exercise to another organisation, "each organisation is responsible for the child".
DECLARE `How the organisation stood to me` IS ONE OF
    `it exercised care, supervision or authority over me, or claimed to, or was obliged by law to`
    `it delegated care, supervision or authority over me, wholly or partly, to another organisation`
    `none of these`

-- s 6E: who is "an individual associated with an organisation". The list is "without limitation" and "includes".
DECLARE `Who the abuser was to the organisation` IS ONE OF
    `an office holder, officer, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor of the organisation`
    `a religious leader or member of the personnel of the organisation, which is a religious organisation`
    `an authorised carer authorised by the organisation as a designated agency under the Children's Guardian Act 2019`
    `someone associated with another organisation to which this organisation delegated care, supervision or authority over me`
    `someone linked to it only because the organisation funds or regulates another organisation`
    `someone else`

-- s 6G: "employee of an organisation includes an individual who is akin to an employee".
DECLARE `How the abuser worked for the organisation` IS ONE OF
    `as its employee`
    `not as its employee, but carrying out activities as an integral part of its activities and for its benefit`
    `in neither of those ways`

-- The answer to "what does section 6F mean for my claim?".
DECLARE `What section 6F means for my claim` IS ONE OF
    `the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty to me, unless it proves it took reasonable precautions`
    `the organisation breached its duty: the presumption stands because it did not prove reasonable precautions`
    `the presumption is rebutted: the court found the organisation took reasonable precautions`
    `section 6F does not apply: the abuse happened before section 6F commenced`
    `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
    `the Act does not settle it`

-- s 6N: what I can do while the organisation has no suitable proper defendant.
DECLARE `What section 6N means for me` IS ONE OF
    `I may apply for the court to appoint the trustees of an associated trust as proper defendant`
    `not yet: the 120 days after service have not ended`
    `no: a suitable proper defendant was appointed in time and is still suitable`
    `no: the State is taken to be the proper defendant for a public sector body`
    `no: section 6N is for unincorporated organisations`

-- s 6N(4): where the organisation stands on its duty to identify its associated trusts.
DECLARE `The organisation's duty to identify its trusts` IS ONE OF
    `the organisation identified its associated trusts within the 28 days`
    `the 28 days have not ended and the organisation has not yet identified its associated trusts`
    `the organisation did not identify its associated trusts within the 28 days`

-- s 7E: what else the court may set aside with an affected agreement.
DECLARE `Thing giving effect to my settlement` IS ONE OF
    `a contract, deed or other agreement`
    `an order or judgment of the court or of a lower court`
    `a deed of release accepting a National Redress Scheme offer, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in the offer`
    `an agreement settling a cross-claim between defendants, or by which one defendant indemnified another`
    `a contract of insurance`

-- The parties and acts of the one regulative rule (s 6N(4)).
DECLARE `Part 1B party` IS ONE OF `the unincorporated organisation`
DECLARE `Part 1B act` IS ONE OF `identify its associated trusts to the court`

§§ `s 6A -- child and organisation`

-- s 6A "child means a person under the age of 18 years"; "organisation ... does not include the State".
GIVEN `the age` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `was a child at` `the age` IF `the age` LESS THAN 18

-- s 6F(5), s 6H(4): the Part 1B meaning of child abuse.
GIVEN `the abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse`, `the act was lawful at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is child abuse within ss 6F and 6H` `the abuse` `the act was lawful at the time` IF
        (    `the abuse` EQUALS `sexual abuse`
          OR `the abuse` EQUALS `physical abuse`)
    AND (NOT `the act was lawful at the time`)

§§ `ss 6D, 6E -- responsibility and association`

-- s 6D, a definition introduced by "if": when neither limb holds, JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the standing` IS A `How the organisation stood to me`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the organisation was responsible for me given` `the standing` IF
    (NOT (`the standing` EQUALS `none of these`))

-- s 6E. (1) "without limitation includes": the listed people are associated; anyone else is open (NOTHING), since the
-- list is not closed and the regulations under s 6E(1)(c) are not deposited. (2) "not associated ... solely because the
-- organisation wholly or partly funds or regulates another organisation": a flat negative, JUST FALSE. (3) a person
-- associated with a delegate organisation "is also taken to be" associated with the delegating one.
GIVEN `the abuser` IS A `Who the abuser was to the organisation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the abuser was associated with the organisation, given` `the abuser` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the abuser`
    WHEN `someone linked to it only because the organisation funds or regulates another organisation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the list is open: s 6E(1) "without limitation includes"; regulations not deposited)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 6F -- the duty to prevent child abuse, and the reverse onus`

-- s 6F(2) "An organisation that has responsibility for a child must take reasonable precautions to prevent an individual
-- associated with the organisation from perpetrating child abuse of the child in connection with the organisation's
-- responsibility for the child." (3) "the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty if the plaintiff
-- establishes that an individual associated with the organisation perpetrated the child abuse in connection with the
-- organisation's responsibility for the child, unless the organisation establishes that it took reasonable
-- precautions". Sch 1 cl 43: "applies only in respect of child abuse perpetrated after the commencement of that
-- section". Abuse on the commencement day is taken as after it (fork F2). Whether the organisation took reasonable
-- precautions (s 6F(4)) is the court's finding.
@export Did the organisation owe me the section 6F duty to prevent the abuse, and is it presumed to have breached it (ss 6A, 6D, 6E, 6F; Sch 1 cl 43)?
GIVEN `the day the abuse happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse you are asking about was perpetrated (for abuse over a period, ask for each day or the earliest)
      `the day section 6F commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day section 6F of the Civil Liability Act commenced, inserted by the Civil Liability Amendment (Organisational Child Abuse Liability) Act 2018 (the commencement date is not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `my age when it happened` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the abuse happened
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse. One of: "sexual abuse", "physical abuse", "another kind of abuse, such as emotional or psychological abuse or neglect"
      `the act was lawful when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was lawful at the time it took place (for example lawful physical punishment at that time); usually no
      `the organisation is the State itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant is the State of New South Wales itself (a government agency or public sector body is not the State itself)
      `how the organisation stood to me` IS A `How the organisation stood to me` @desc How the organisation stood to you. One of: "it exercised care, supervision or authority over me, or claimed to, or was obliged by law to"; "it delegated care, supervision or authority over me, wholly or partly, to another organisation"; "none of these"
      `who the abuser was` IS A `Who the abuser was to the organisation` @desc Who the abuser was to the organisation. One of: "an office holder, officer, employee, owner, volunteer or contractor of the organisation"; "a religious leader or member of the personnel of the organisation, which is a religious organisation"; "an authorised carer authorised by the organisation as a designated agency under the Children's Guardian Act 2019"; "someone associated with another organisation to which this organisation delegated care, supervision or authority over me"; "someone linked to it only because the organisation funds or regulates another organisation"; "someone else"
      `the abuse was connected with its responsibility for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuse was perpetrated in connection with the organisation's care, supervision or authority over you
      `the court's finding on reasonable precautions` IS A `The court's finding` @desc Whether the court has found that the organisation took reasonable precautions to prevent the abuse. One of: "the court has found that it is so", "the court has found that it is not so", "the court has not decided"
GIVETH A `What section 6F means for my claim`
`What does section 6F mean for my claim` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day the abuse happened` `is before` `the day section 6F commenced` THEN `section 6F does not apply: the abuse happened before section 6F commenced`
           IF (NOT `was a child at` `my age when it happened`) THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF (NOT `is child abuse within ss 6F and 6H` `the kind of abuse` `the act was lawful when it happened`) THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF `the organisation is the State itself` THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF (NOT `the organisation was responsible for me given` `how the organisation stood to me`) THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF (NOT `the abuse was connected with its responsibility for me`) THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF `the abuser was associated with the organisation, given` `who the abuser was` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN `section 6F gives me no claim on these facts`
           IF `the abuser was associated with the organisation, given` `who the abuser was` EQUALS NOTHING THEN `the Act does not settle it` -- NOTHING-kind (s 6E's open list)
           IF `the court's finding on reasonable precautions` EQUALS `the court has found that it is so` THEN `the presumption is rebutted: the court found the organisation took reasonable precautions`
           IF `the court's finding on reasonable precautions` EQUALS `the court has found that it is not so` THEN `the organisation breached its duty: the presumption stands because it did not prove reasonable precautions`
           OTHERWISE `the organisation is presumed to have breached its duty to me, unless it proves it took reasonable precautions`

§§ `ss 6G, 6H -- vicarious liability`

-- s 6G(2) "akin to an employee ... if the individual carries out activities as an integral part of the activities
-- carried on by the organisation and does so for the benefit of the organisation"; (3) "However, ... not akin to an
-- employee if (a) the activities are carried out for a recognisably independent business ... or (b) ... the activities
-- of an authorised carer". Regulations under s 6G(4) are not deposited.
GIVEN `the working` IS A `How the abuser worked for the organisation`
      `independent business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `authorised carer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the abuser was an employee within s 6G, given` `the working` `independent business` `authorised carer` IF
    CONSIDER `the working`
    WHEN `as its employee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `not as its employee, but carrying out activities as an integral part of its activities and for its benefit` THEN
        (NOT `independent business`) AND (NOT `authorised carer`)
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 6H(1) "An organisation is vicariously liable for child abuse perpetrated against a child by an employee of the
-- organisation if (a) the apparent performance by the employee of a role in which the organisation placed the employee
-- supplies the occasion for the perpetration of the child abuse by the employee, and (b) the employee takes advantage
-- of that occasion". (a) is the court's finding, made with s 6H(2) in mind (authority, power or control; trust; the
-- ability to achieve intimacy). (3) "in addition to, the common law": a JUST FALSE here means "section 6H gives no
-- vicarious liability on these facts", never "no vicarious liability at all". Sch 1 cl 44: only abuse after
-- commencement.
@export Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H for the abuse its employee (or someone akin to an employee) did to me (ss 6G, 6H; Sch 1 cl 44)?
GIVEN `the day the abuse happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the abuse you are asking about was perpetrated
      `the day section 6H commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day section 6H of the Civil Liability Act commenced, inserted by the Civil Liability Amendment (Organisational Child Abuse Liability) Act 2018 (the commencement date is not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `my age when it happened` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the abuse happened
      `the kind of abuse` IS A `Kind of abuse` @desc The kind of abuse. One of: "sexual abuse", "physical abuse", "another kind of abuse, such as emotional or psychological abuse or neglect"
      `the act was lawful when it happened` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the act was lawful at the time it took place; usually no
      `the organisation is the State itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant is the State of New South Wales itself (a government agency or public sector body is not the State itself)
      `how the abuser worked for it` IS A `How the abuser worked for the organisation` @desc How the abuser worked for the organisation. One of: "as its employee"; "not as its employee, but carrying out activities as an integral part of its activities and for its benefit" (for example a priest, or a volunteer embedded in its work); "in neither of those ways"
      `the activities were for an independent business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser's activities were carried out for a recognisably independent business of the abuser or of someone else
      `the abuser was acting as an authorised carer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activities were those of an authorised carer (a foster carer under the Children and Young Persons (Care and Protection) Act 1998), carried on in that capacity
      `the court's finding that the role supplied the occasion` IS A `The court's finding` @desc Whether the court has found that the apparent performance of a role the organisation placed the abuser in supplied the occasion for the abuse (the court looks at whether the role gave authority, power or control over you, your trust, or the ability to achieve intimacy with you). One of: "the court has found that it is so", "the court has found that it is not so", "the court has not decided"
      `the abuser took advantage of that occasion` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the abuser took advantage of that occasion to abuse you
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the organisation vicariously liable under section 6H` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the day the abuse happened` `is before` `the day section 6H commenced` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `was a child at` `my age when it happened`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `is child abuse within ss 6F and 6H` `the kind of abuse` `the act was lawful when it happened`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the organisation is the State itself` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the abuser was an employee within s 6G, given` `how the abuser worked for it` `the activities were for an independent business` `the abuser was acting as an authorised carer`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the abuser took advantage of that occasion`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the court's finding that the role supplied the occasion` EQUALS `the court has found that it is not so` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the court's finding that the role supplied the occasion` EQUALS `the court has found that it is so` THEN JUST TRUE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the court has not decided the s 6H(1)(a) question)

§§ `Division 4 -- unincorporated organisations and proper defendants`

-- s 6K(1) "Child abuse proceedings may be commenced or continue against an unincorporated organisation in the name of
-- the organisation ... as if the organisation had legal personality." s 6J "child abuse proceedings means proceedings
-- for a civil claim arising from abuse (including sexual abuse) against a child, whether arising under this Part or the
-- common law". Sch 1 cl 45: Division 4 "extends to ... abuse perpetrated before the commencement of that Division". For
-- an incorporated organisation the Division says nothing (it can be sued anyway): NOTHING.
@export Can I sue an unincorporated organisation in its own name for abuse I suffered as a child (ss 6J, 6K; Sch 1 cl 45)?
GIVEN `the organisation is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is incorporated (a company, an incorporated association, a body corporate); churches, clubs and associations are often not
      `my age when it happened` IS A NUMBER @desc Your age in whole years when the abuse happened
      `my claim arises from abuse against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your civil claim arises from abuse (of any kind, including sexual abuse) against you, under Part 1B or the common law
      `the organisation is the State itself` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the defendant is the State of New South Wales itself
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can I sue the unincorporated organisation in its own name` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the organisation is the State itself` THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the organisation is incorporated` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (scope limit: Division 4 is about unincorporated organisations; an incorporated one is sued under the general law)
           IF (NOT `was a child at` `my age when it happened`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `my claim arises from abuse against me`) THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 6M "an entity is suitable to be appointed as a proper defendant ... if (a) the entity is able to be sued in this
-- State, and (b) the entity (or, if the entity is a trustee of a trust, the trust) has sufficient assets in this State
-- to satisfy any judgment or order".
@export Is this entity (for example a company or the trustees of a trust) suitable to be the proper defendant for the unincorporated organisation (s 6M)?
GIVEN `it can be sued in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity can be sued in New South Wales
      `it has enough assets in New South Wales` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity (or, for a trustee, the trust) has assets in New South Wales sufficient to satisfy any judgment or order that may arise from your proceedings
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is the entity a suitable proper defendant` MEANS
    IF `it can be sued in New South Wales` AND `it has enough assets in New South Wales`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 6N(3) "A trust is an associated trust of an unincorporated organisation ... if one or more of the following apply";
-- (g) counts only "if the trust has been established or used for the activities of the organisation or for the benefit
-- of the organisation".
@export Is this trust an associated trust of the unincorporated organisation, whose trustees could be made the proper defendant (s 6N(3))?
GIVEN `it controls the trust's income or property` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has, directly or indirectly, the power to control the application of the trust's income or the distribution of its property
      `it can obtain the benefit of the trust` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has the power to obtain the beneficial enjoyment of the trust's property or income, with or without anyone else's consent
      `it can appoint or remove the trustees` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has, directly or indirectly, the power to appoint or remove the trustee or trustees
      `it can appoint or remove beneficiaries` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has, directly or indirectly, the power to appoint or remove beneficiaries of the trust
      `the trustee follows its directions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trustee is accustomed, or obliged (formally or informally), to act according to the organisation's directions, instructions or wishes
      `it decides the trust's other operations` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has, directly or indirectly, the power to determine the outcome of any other decisions about the trust's operations
      `a member or manager holds such a power under the deed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a member or management member of the organisation has one of those powers under the trust deed
      `the trust was set up or used for the organisation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the trust has been established or used for the organisation's activities or benefit (this matters only for a power held by a member or manager)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is it an associated trust` MEANS
    IF    `it controls the trust's income or property`
       OR `it can obtain the benefit of the trust`
       OR `it can appoint or remove the trustees`
       OR `it can appoint or remove beneficiaries`
       OR `the trustee follows its directions`
       OR `it decides the trust's other operations`
       OR (`a member or manager holds such a power under the deed` AND `the trust was set up or used for the organisation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 6N(1) "This section applies if (a) child abuse proceedings are commenced against an unincorporated organisation and no
-- suitable proper defendant is appointed for the organisation by the end of 120 days after the unincorporated
-- organisation (or a management member ...) is served with notice of the commencement of the proceedings, or (b) after
-- that time, the proper defendant appointed ceases to be a suitable proper defendant." (2) the court may, "on the
-- application of the plaintiff", appoint the trustees of an associated trust. s 6L(3): for a public sector body "the
-- State is taken to be appointed as the proper defendant" (taken as suitable: fork F3). The service day is day 0; the
-- 120 days end at the end of day 120, so an appointment on day 120 is in time and the earliest application is day 121
-- (fork F4).
GIVEN `the day served` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for appointing a proper defendant after` `the day served` MEANS `the day` 120 `days after` `the day served`

@export By when must the unincorporated organisation have a suitable proper defendant appointed, before I can ask the court to appoint its trusts' trustees (s 6N(1))?
GIVEN `the day the organisation was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the unincorporated organisation (or a member of its management committee or someone who takes part in its management) was served with notice that your proceedings had started
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must a proper defendant be appointed` MEANS `the last day for appointing a proper defendant after` `the day the organisation was served`

@export Can I apply now for the court to appoint the trustees of the organisation's associated trusts as its proper defendant (ss 6L, 6N(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the organisation is incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is incorporated
      `it is a public sector body` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation is a public sector body (a government sector agency, a statutory body representing the Crown that employs staff or received State funding, or a body that replaced or was one of those)
      `the day the organisation was served` IS A DATE @desc The day the unincorporated organisation (or one of its management members) was served with notice that your proceedings had started
      `a suitable proper defendant has been appointed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has appointed a proper defendant that is suitable (can be sued in NSW and has enough assets in NSW)
      `the day it was appointed` IS A DATE @desc The day that proper defendant was appointed (any day if none was)
      `it has since ceased to be suitable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether that proper defendant has since ceased to be suitable
      `the day I would apply` IS A DATE @desc The day you would make your application to the court
GIVETH A `What section 6N means for me`
`Can I apply for the trustees to be appointed` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the organisation is incorporated` THEN `no: section 6N is for unincorporated organisations`
           IF `it is a public sector body` THEN `no: the State is taken to be the proper defendant for a public sector body`
           IF (NOT (`the deadline` `is before` `the day I would apply`)) THEN `not yet: the 120 days after service have not ended`
           IF     `a suitable proper defendant has been appointed`
              AND (NOT (`the deadline` `is before` `the day it was appointed`))
              AND (NOT `it has since ceased to be suitable`)
           THEN `no: a suitable proper defendant was appointed in time and is still suitable`
           OTHERWISE `I may apply for the court to appoint the trustees of an associated trust as proper defendant`
    WHERE
        `the deadline` MEANS `the last day for appointing a proper defendant after` `the day the organisation was served`

-- s 6N(4) "On the making of an application by a plaintiff under this section, the unincorporated organisation must,
-- within 28 days after the application is made, identify to the court any associated trusts of the organisation,
-- including by identifying the financial capacity of those trusts." A duty with a deadline: a regulative rule. Day 0 is
-- the day of the application; the last day is day 28.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Part 1B party` `Part 1B act`
`s 6N(4) -- the organisation must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `the unincorporated organisation`
    MUST `identify its associated trusts to the court`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST BREACH BY `the unincorporated organisation` BECAUSE "associated trusts not identified to the court within 28 days after the plaintiff's application (s 6N(4))"

@export By when must the unincorporated organisation identify its associated trusts to the court, after my application (s 6N(4))?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied to the court under section 6N for trustees to be appointed as proper defendant
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must the organisation identify its trusts` MEANS `the day` 28 `days after` `the day I applied`

@export Has the unincorporated organisation met its duty to identify its associated trusts within 28 days of my application (s 6N(4))?
GIVEN `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day you applied to the court under section 6N for trustees to be appointed as proper defendant
      `it has identified its trusts` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the organisation has identified its associated trusts (and their financial capacity) to the court
      `the day it identified them` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any day if it has not); not later than today
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `The organisation's duty to identify its trusts`
`Has the organisation identified its trusts in time` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the trace`
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN `the organisation identified its associated trusts within the 28 days`
    OTHERWISE
        IF (NOT `it has identified its trusts`) AND `the days from` `the day I applied` `to` `today` AT MOST 28
        THEN `the 28 days have not ended and the organisation has not yet identified its associated trusts`
        ELSE `the organisation did not identify its associated trusts within the 28 days`
    WHERE
        `the trace` MEANS
            IF `it has identified its trusts`
            THEN EVALTRACE `s 6N(4) -- the organisation must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` 0 (LIST (EVENT `the unincorporated organisation` `identify its associated trusts to the court` (`the days from` `the day I applied` `to` `the day it identified them`)), (WAITUNTIL (`the days from` `the day I applied` `to` `today`)))
            ELSE EVALTRACE `s 6N(4) -- the organisation must identify its associated trusts within 28 days` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL (`the days from` `the day I applied` `to` `today`)))

-- s 6P(2) "Liability of a trustee of an associated trust incurred by the trustee as a proper defendant in child abuse
-- proceedings is limited to the value of the trust property." (6) that liability "includes any unpaid judgment debt ...,
-- any amount paid in settlement ... and any costs".
@export What is the most I can recover from the trustees of an associated trust appointed as proper defendant (s 6P(2), (6))?
GIVEN `what the organisation would owe me` IS A NUMBER @desc The amount the organisation would be liable for in your proceedings, in dollars: the judgment or settlement and any costs
      `the value of the trust property` IS A NUMBER @desc The value of the trust's property, in dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`The most I can recover from the trustees` MEANS
    `the lesser of` `what the organisation would owe me` `and` `the value of the trust property`

§§ `Part 1C -- setting aside settlements`

-- s 7C(1) "an affected agreement means an agreement that prevents the exercise of an action on a cause of action to
-- which section 6A of the Limitation Act 1969 applies, if the agreement occurred (a) before the commencement of that
-- section, and at the time of the agreement, a limitation period applying to the cause of action had expired, or (b)
-- before the commencement of Part 1B ..., and at the time of the agreement, an organisation, that would have been liable
-- under Part 1B ... had the Part been in force, was not incorporated, or (c) before the commencement of Part 1B ..., and
-- the agreement is not just and reasonable in the circumstances." (2) a period "is taken to have expired even if it were
-- possible at the time to seek the leave of a court to extend the period". A "means ... if" definition: when no limb
-- holds, JUST FALSE; limb (c) is the court's finding, so it can leave the answer open.
@export Is my earlier settlement of my child abuse claim an "affected agreement" that the court can be asked to set aside (s 7C)?
GIVEN `my claim is one Limitation Act section 6A applies to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action is one to which section 6A of the Limitation Act 1969 applies (an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse: sexual abuse, serious physical abuse, or other abuse connected with it)
      `the agreement stops me suing on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement agreement prevents you from bringing an action on that cause of action
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day the settlement agreement was made
      `the day Limitation Act section 6A commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day section 6A of the Limitation Act 1969 commenced (not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `the day Part 1B commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day Part 1B of the Civil Liability Act commenced (not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `the limitation period had expired when I settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the agreement, a limitation period for your claim had expired (count it as expired even if you could then have asked a court for leave to extend it)
      `the liable organisation was unincorporated when I settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the agreement, an organisation that would have been liable to you under Part 1B (had it then been in force) was not incorporated
      `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable` IS A `The court's finding` @desc Whether the court has found that the agreement is not just and reasonable in the circumstances. One of: "the court has found that it is so", "the court has found that it is not so", "the court has not decided"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Is my settlement an affected agreement` MEANS
    BRANCH IF (NOT `my claim is one Limitation Act section 6A applies to`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF (NOT `the agreement stops me suing on it`) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the day of the agreement` `is before` `the day Limitation Act section 6A commenced` AND `the limitation period had expired when I settled` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF (NOT (`the day of the agreement` `is before` `the day Part 1B commenced`)) THEN JUST FALSE
           IF `the liable organisation was unincorporated when I settled` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable` EQUALS `the court has found that it is so` THEN JUST TRUE
           IF `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable` EQUALS `the court has found that it is not so` THEN JUST FALSE
           OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the court has not decided whether the agreement is just and reasonable, s 7C(1)(c))

-- s 7D(1) the applicant "may (a) commence proceedings on the cause of action ... and (b) apply to the court to set aside
-- the affected agreement"; (2) "The court may set aside an affected agreement if it is just and reasonable to do so."
@export Can the court set aside my earlier child abuse settlement so that I can sue (ss 7C, 7D)?
GIVEN `my claim is one Limitation Act section 6A applies to` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your cause of action is one to which section 6A of the Limitation Act 1969 applies (an action for damages for death or personal injury resulting from child abuse)
      `the agreement stops me suing on it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the settlement agreement prevents you from bringing an action on that cause of action
      `the day of the agreement` IS A DATE @desc The day the settlement agreement was made
      `the day Limitation Act section 6A commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day section 6A of the Limitation Act 1969 commenced (not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `the day Part 1B commenced` IS A DATE @desc The day Part 1B of the Civil Liability Act commenced (not in the deposited text; check the NSW legislation website)
      `the limitation period had expired when I settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the agreement, a limitation period for your claim had expired (even if you could then have asked for leave to extend it)
      `the liable organisation was unincorporated when I settled` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when you made the agreement, an organisation that would have been liable to you under Part 1B was not incorporated
      `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable` IS A `The court's finding` @desc Whether the court has found that the agreement is not just and reasonable in the circumstances. One of: "the court has found that it is so", "the court has found that it is not so", "the court has not decided"
      `the court's finding that setting it aside is just and reasonable` IS A `The court's finding` @desc Whether the court has found that it is just and reasonable to set the agreement aside (it may weigh the amount you were paid, the parties' bargaining positions, and the conduct of the other parties and their lawyers). One of: "the court has found that it is so", "the court has found that it is not so", "the court has not decided"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court set aside my settlement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `Is my settlement an affected agreement` `my claim is one Limitation Act section 6A applies to` `the agreement stops me suing on it` `the day of the agreement` `the day Limitation Act section 6A commenced` `the day Part 1B commenced` `the limitation period had expired when I settled` `the liable organisation was unincorporated when I settled` `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE
    OTHERWISE
        IF `the court's finding that setting it aside is just and reasonable` EQUALS `the court has found that it is not so`
        THEN JUST FALSE
        ELSE IF `the court's finding that setting it aside is just and reasonable` EQUALS `the court has found that it is so`
             THEN `Is my settlement an affected agreement` `my claim is one Limitation Act section 6A applies to` `the agreement stops me suing on it` `the day of the agreement` `the day Limitation Act section 6A commenced` `the day Part 1B commenced` `the limitation period had expired when I settled` `the liable organisation was unincorporated when I settled` `the court's finding that the agreement is not just and reasonable`
             ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the court has not decided whether setting the agreement aside is just and reasonable, s 7D(2))

-- s 7E(1) "If the court decides to set aside an affected agreement ..., it may also set aside any of the following that
-- gives effect to the agreement (a) a contract, deed or other agreement, (b) an order or judgment"; (2) "However, the
-- court must not set aside" a National Redress Scheme deed of release (and a prior-payment agreement taken into account
-- in the offer), a cross-claim settlement or indemnity between defendants (to that extent), or a contract of insurance.
@export If the court sets aside my settlement, can it also set aside this other thing that gives effect to it (s 7E)?
GIVEN `the court has set aside my settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has decided to set aside your settlement (the affected agreement) under Part 1C
      `the thing` IS A `Thing giving effect to my settlement` @desc What else you want set aside. One of: "a contract, deed or other agreement"; "an order or judgment of the court or of a lower court"; "a deed of release accepting a National Redress Scheme offer, or an agreement about a prior payment taken into account in the offer"; "an agreement settling a cross-claim between defendants, or by which one defendant indemnified another"; "a contract of insurance"
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Can the court also set aside this thing` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the court has set aside my settlement`)
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the thing`
         WHEN `a contract, deed or other agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an order or judgment of the court or of a lower court` THEN JUST TRUE
         OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 7F(3) "An amount paid, including legal costs or disbursements, or other consideration given under the affected
-- agreement (a) is not recoverable despite the agreement being void, and (b) may be taken into account by a court in
-- determining damages". A flat negative for a set-aside agreement; where nothing has been set aside the Act says
-- nothing about repayment.
@export If my settlement is set aside, can the other side make me pay back what I received under it (s 7F(3))?
GIVEN `the court has set aside my settlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the court has set aside your settlement (the affected agreement) under Part 1C
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Must I repay what I received under the settlement` MEANS
    IF `the court has set aside my settlement`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (the text is silent: s 7F speaks only of an agreement set aside)
